This product bundles third-party software and assets under their own licenses.

The native library `libgoldberry` STATICALLY LINKS the following, so their
code is present in every binary artifact Goldberry distributes:

  Blend2D        Zlib license      https://blend2d.com
  AsmJit         Zlib license      https://asmjit.com          (via Blend2D)
  SDL3           Zlib license      https://www.libsdl.org
  Yoga           MIT license       https://www.yogalayout.dev
  HarfBuzz       MIT license       https://harfbuzz.github.io
  md4c           MIT license       https://github.com/mity/md4c
  libwebp        BSD-3-Clause      https://github.com/webmproject/libwebp

The OPTIONAL sibling library `libgoldberry-webview` compiles in one more, and
brings no browser engine of its own (the operating system's is used):

  webview/webview MIT license      https://github.com/webview/webview

The following assets are embedded in goldberry-core:

  Inter                SIL Open Font License 1.1   https://rsms.me/inter/
  JetBrains Mono       SIL Open Font License 1.1   https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/
  Lucide               ISC; MIT for Feather icons  https://lucide.dev

And one is embedded in goldberry-emoji, which is an OPTIONAL artifact:

  Noto Color Emoji     SIL Open Font License 1.1   https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji

Noto Color Emoji is in an artifact of its own because it is five megabytes an
application that never draws an emoji should not carry.
The face shipped is Google's COLRv1 build, release v2.057, unmodified. The
Apache-2.0 licence of Goldberry's own code is unaffected — the font is an
embedded asset, not linked code.

The media engine's natives ship in goldberry-media's natives-<platform>
classifier jars, which are also OPTIONAL: an application adds them by name,
and nothing else needs them. One shared library, libgoldberry-media,
STATICALLY LINKS:

  dav1d          BSD-2-Clause      https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d
  libvpx         BSD-3-Clause      https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libvpx
  Opus           BSD-3-Clause      https://opus-codec.org
  libogg         BSD-3-Clause      https://xiph.org/ogg
  libvorbis      BSD-3-Clause      https://xiph.org/vorbis
  libtheora      BSD-3-Clause      https://theora.org
  FLAC           BSD-3-Clause      https://xiph.org/flac          (libFLAC)
  libyuv         BSD-3-Clause      https://chromium.googlesource.com/libyuv/libyuv
  minimp3        CC0-1.0           https://github.com/lieff/minimp3

Each natives jar carries META-INF/media-NOTICE.txt naming the nine at the tags
and commits that were built. No patent-pool codec is built into them.
goldberry-media's system decoders, which decode H.264, HEVC, AAC,
AC-3 and E-AC-3, bundle nothing: they call the decoders the operating system
has, under the licences those were installed under.

Full licence texts and per-component attribution are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
and the licenses/ directory.
